  {
    "jd_id": "JD-038",
    "jd_title": "Junior CloudOps / SysOps Engineer Linux",
    "company_name": "Teamwork Vietnam Ltd",
    "domain_category": "DevOps",
    "job_level": "Intern",
    "original_jd_text": "Giới thiệu công ty\nThu nhập:\nCạnh tranh\nLoại hình:\nToàn thời gian\nChức vụ:\nThực tập sinh\nKinh nghiệm:\n0,5 - 2 năm\nphần mềm\nlinux\ncloud\nautomation\nMô tả công việc\nMô tả Công việc\nAre you passionate about Linux, cloud technologies, automation, or infrastructure engineering?\nJoin our CloudOps Team and work alongside experienced engineers supporting enterprise environments for international customers. This is an excellent opportunity for graduates and junior IT professionals who want to build a career in Cloud Engineering, DevOps, Site Reliability Engineering (SRE), or Platform Operations.\nYou'll receive hands-on training, real-world operational experience, and mentorship while working with modern cloud and infrastructure technologies.\nWhat You'll Be Doing\nMonitor and support enterprise cloud and infrastructure environments\nTroubleshoot Linux, cloud, virtualization, and system-related issues\nAssist with infrastructure automation and operational improvements\nParticipate in incident response and problem resolution activities\nCollaborate with senior engineers to maintain service reliability and performance\nFollow ITIL-based operational processes and best practices\nContinuously learn and develop technical expertise across cloud and infrastructure technologies\nWhat You'll Learn & Work With\nLinux & Infrastructure\nEnterprise Linux administration\nSystem monitoring and troubleshooting\nProduction operations and support\nCloud Technologies\nAWS cloud infrastructure and operations\nCloud-native operational practices\nResource provisioning and management\nVirtualization Platforms\nVMware\nProxmox\nXen\nNutanix\nAutomation & DevOps\nShell/Bash scripting\nAnsible\nTerraform\nInfrastructure as Code (IaC)\nOperations Excellence\nIncident management and root cause analysis\nService monitoring and observability\nITIL operational best practices\nYêu cầu\nYêu Cầu Công Việc\nRequired Qualifications\nBachelor's degree in computer science, Information Technology, or a related field (or equivalent practical experience)\nBasic knowledge of Linux from coursework, personal projects, internships, homelabs, or self-study\nBasic scripting experience (Bash, Shell, Python, or similar)\nStrong analytical and problem-solving skills\nEagerness to learn new technologies and continuously improve\nTeam player with good communication skills\nCustomer-focused mindset with a strong sense of ownership and responsibility\nAbility to communicate effectively in English\nNice to Have\nWe don't expect candidates to have everything below. Any exposure is a plus:\nAWS or other cloud platform experience\nKnowledge of virtualization technologies such as VMware, Proxmox, Xen, or Nutanix\nUnderstanding of networking fundamentals (TCP/IP, DNS, routing, firewalls)\nExperience with Ansible, Terraform, or similar automation tools\nFamiliarity with Git, Docker, Kubernetes, or CI/CD concepts\nLinux or cloud certifications (RHCSA, LPIC, AWS Cloud Practitioner, etc.)\nParticipation in internships, university projects, homelabs, personal projects, or open-source contributions.\nQuyền lợi\nLaptop\nChế độ bảo hiểm\nDu Lịch\nPhụ cấp\nDu lịch nước ngoài\nĐồng phục\nChế độ thưởng\nChăm sóc sức khỏe\nĐào tạo\nTăng lương\nCông tác phí\nPhụ cấp thâm niên\nNghỉ phép năm\nCLB thể thao",
    "requirements_text": "Bachelor's degree in computer science, Information Technology, or a related field (or equivalent practical experience)\nBasic knowledge of Linux from coursework, personal projects, internships, homelabs, or self-study\nBasic scripting experience (Bash, Shell, Python, or similar)\nStrong analytical and problem-solving skills\nEagerness to learn new technologies and continuously improve\nTeam player with good communication skills\nCustomer-focused mindset with a strong sense of ownership and responsibility\nAbility to communicate effectively in English\nNice to Have\nWe don't expect candidates to have everything below. Any exposure is a plus:\nAWS or other cloud platform experience\nKnowledge of virtualization technologies such as VMware, Proxmox, Xen, or Nutanix\nUnderstanding of networking fundamentals (TCP/IP, DNS, routing, firewalls)\nExperience with Ansible, Terraform, or similar automation tools\nFamiliarity with Git, Docker, Kubernetes, or CI/CD concepts\nLinux or cloud certifications (RHCSA, LPIC, AWS Cloud Practitioner, etc.)\nParticipation in internships, university projects, homelabs, personal projects, or open-source contributions.",
    "review_status": "PENDING",
