  {
    "jd_id": "JD-078",
    "jd_title": "HCM – Junior Fullstack Developer (ReactJS + NodeJS)",
    "company_name": "Vexere.com - Vietnam’s #1 Transportation Booking Platform (Bus | Flight | Train | Bike Car Rental))",
    "domain_category": "DevOps",
    "job_level": "Intern",
    "original_jd_text": "Junior Fullstack Developer (ReactJS + NodeJS)\nAbout VeXeRe – Revolutionizing The Way Vietnam Travels\nVeXeRe is Vietnam’s No.1 online bus ticketing platform, connecting over 2,000 transport operators and serving millions of passengers every month. We pioneer technology to modernize the transportation industry, bringing users a fast, seamless, and optimized booking experience.\nBeyond buses, VeXeRe is expanding into flights, trains, and car rentals — giving travelers complete freedom of choice for every journey.\nOur Culture\nAt VeXeRe, we believe our mission is to solve real-world social problems through technology. Our culture is built on openness, collaboration, and community spirit. Every member is encouraged to think freely, share ideas, and take ownership — with the opportunity to grow into future leaders.\nOur Vision\nWe aim to become a continuously innovating tech company that revolutionizes transportation and travel across Southeast Asia through AI-native solutions. Every experience — from customer journeys to internal systems — is being reimagined to be smarter, faster, and more human.\nWhy Join Us\nJoining VeXeRe means being part of a young, energetic, and ambitious tech team where you’ll have the freedom to experiment, learn from top engineers, and grow rapidly as we scale.\nAbout The Role\nAre you ready to grow from a developer into a system builder?\nAt VeXeRe, you’ll learn how to design, build, and scale applications that serve millions of users nationwide — all while working with experienced mentors who’ll guide you every step of the way.\nWe’re building a modern microservices-based ecosystem with\nCI/CD, containerization, and cloud infrastructure\n, where you’ll get real hands-on experience with production-level systems.\nOur Tech Stack\nBackend: Node.js, Express.js, RabbitMQ / Kafka, PostgreSQL / Redis / Elasticsearch, Docker / Kubernetes / Jenkins\nFrontend: React.js, ES6 / TypeScript, Redux / Redux-Saga / Hooks\nResponsibilities\nDevelop high-quality solutions to meet business requirements by designing, coding, and shipping well-structured, maintainable software.\nIdentify and address technical debt & challenges: Proactively analyze areas for improvement and implement changes to enhance system performance and scalability.\nCollaborate and share knowledge within the Frontend Squad to maximize team expertise and personal growth.\nTake ownership: Lead a team or a product if capable, contributing to technical direction and best practices.\nRequirements\nMust-Have:\nProactive mindset, curiosity, and a drive to learn.\nFast learner, able to adapt quickly to new technologies.\n2 – 3 years of hands-on experience in software development (frontend ).\nFamiliarity with macOS or Linux for development and deployment tasks.\nUnderstanding of our technology stack (no need to master everything, but familiarity is required):\nBackend: Node.js, PostgreSQL, Redis, Elasticsearch.\nFrontend: React.js, Redux, Redux-Saga, Reselect, React Hooks.\nCommitment to code quality:\nStrong experience in code reviews.\nFamiliarity with unit testing best practices.\nGrowth mindset: Ready to grow rapidly as the company scales several times a year.\nNice-to-Have (Plus)\nSolid foundation in computer science (data structures, algorithms).\nExperience with Docker, CI/CD pipelines, or microservices architecture.\nPrevious experience building and shipping real-world applications.\nBenefits\nCompetitive Compensation & Bonuses\nAttractive salary package with performance-based monthly bonuses (up to 2 months’ salary per year).\n100% salary during the probation period.\nPerformance reviews twice a year with opportunities for salary adjustments.\nFlexible Work & Growth Opportunities\nHybrid working model (work from home or at the office).\nLearn directly from our CTO, Tech Leads, and Senior Engineers.\nBuild your public tech profile by:\nWriting on Medium & VeXeRe Tech Blog under your own name.\nContributing to VeXeRe’s open-source projects.\nSpeaking at internal or public tech talks.\nAttractive stock options for long-term contributors.\nExclusive Employee Perks\nUp to 30% discount on bus tickets for Vexere employees and their families.\n12 annual leave days + 1 additional day every 3 years (convertible to salary).\nVibrant and friendly working environment.\nTraining sessions on soft skills, communication, and modern technologies.\nExciting company activities: team building trips, year-end parties, and more.\nWhat factors can help you trust Vexere?\nVeXeRe is the largest intercity bus booking platform in Vietnam, partnering with over 1,000 bus operators across 3,000 domestic and cross-border routes.\nOur Bus Management System (BMS) is trusted by 700+ transport companies nationwide, helping them modernize operations and boost efficiency.\nWe’re backed by prestigious investors including\nWoowa Brothers (Baemin), CyberAgent Ventures (Japan), BonAngels (Korea), Pix Vine Capital (Singapore), Spiral Ventures (Japan), Access Ventures (Korea), and NCore Ventures (Korea)\n— two of which are\nDecacorns\nvalued over USD 10 billion.\nReview about Vexere\nFor More Information, Please Contact Us Via\nSend your resume to careers@vexere.com\nSubject line: [Full name] – Junior Fullstack Developer\nOr contact Mr. Nhật Anh (Zalo: 0966.197.741) for more details.\nAddress: 2nd Floor, H3 Building, 384 Hoang Dieu, Khanh Hoi Ward, Ho Chi Minh City (District 4)\nWorking Hours: 8:30 AM – 6:00 PM (Mon–Fri) and Saturday mornings, hybrid model.",
    "requirements_text": "VeXeRe is Vietnam’s No.1 online bus ticketing platform, connecting over 2,000 transport operators and serving millions of passengers every month. We pioneer technology to modernize the transportation industry, bringing users a fast, seamless, and optimized booking experience.\nBeyond buses, VeXeRe is expanding into flights, trains, and car rentals — giving travelers complete freedom of choice for every journey.\nAt VeXeRe, we believe our mission is to solve real-world social problems through technology. Our culture is built on openness, collaboration, and community spirit. Every member is encouraged to think freely, share ideas, and take ownership — with the opportunity to grow into future leaders.\nWe aim to become a continuously innovating tech company that revolutionizes transportation and travel across Southeast Asia through AI-native solutions. Every experience — from customer journeys to internal systems — is being reimagined to be smarter, faster, and more human.\nJoining VeXeRe means being part of a young, energetic, and ambitious tech team where you’ll have the freedom to experiment, learn from top engineers, and grow rapidly as we scale.\nBackend: Node.js, Express.js, RabbitMQ / Kafka, PostgreSQL / Redis / Elasticsearch, Docker / Kubernetes / Jenkins\nFrontend: React.js, ES6 / TypeScript, Redux / Redux-Saga / Hooks\nDevelop high-quality solutions to meet business requirements by designing, coding, and shipping well-structured, maintainable software.\nIdentify and address technical debt & challenges: Proactively analyze areas for improvement and implement changes to enhance system performance and scalability.\nCollaborate and share knowledge within the Frontend Squad to maximize team expertise and personal growth.\nTake ownership: Lead a team or a product if capable, contributing to technical direction and best practices.\nProactive mindset, curiosity, and a drive to learn.\nFast learner, able to adapt quickly to new technologies.\n2 – 3 years of hands-on experience in software development (frontend ).\nFamiliarity with macOS or Linux for development and deployment tasks.\nUnderstanding of our technology stack (no need to master everything, but familiarity is required):\nBackend: Node.js, PostgreSQL, Redis, Elasticsearch.\nFrontend: React.js, Redux, Redux-Saga, Reselect, React Hooks.\nCommitment to code quality:\nStrong experience in code reviews.\nFamiliarity with unit testing best practices.\nGrowth mindset: Ready to grow rapidly as the company scales several times a year.\nSolid foundation in computer science (data structures, algorithms).\nExperience with Docker, CI/CD pipelines, or microservices architecture.\nPrevious experience building and shipping real-world applications.\nAttractive salary package with performance-based monthly bonuses (up to 2 months’ salary per year).\n100% salary during the probation period.\nPerformance reviews twice a year with opportunities for salary adjustments.\nHybrid working model (work from home or at the office).\nLearn directly from our CTO, Tech Leads, and Senior Engineers.\nBuild your public tech profile by:\nWriting on Medium & VeXeRe Tech Blog under your own name.\nContributing to VeXeRe’s open-source projects.\nSpeaking at internal or public tech talks.\nAttractive stock options for long-term contributors.\nUp to 30% discount on bus tickets for Vexere employees and their families.\n12 annual leave days + 1 additional day every 3 years (convertible to salary).\nVibrant and friendly working environment.\nTraining sessions on soft skills, communication, and modern technologies.\nExciting company activities: team building trips, year-end parties, and more.\nSend your resume to careers@vexere.com\nSubject line: [Full name] – Junior Fullstack Developer\nOr contact Mr. Nhật Anh (Zalo: 0966.197.741) for more details.\nAddress: 2nd Floor, H3 Building, 384 Hoang Dieu, Khanh Hoi Ward, Ho Chi Minh City (District 4)\nWorking Hours: 8:30 AM – 6:00 PM (Mon–Fri) and Saturday mornings, hybrid model.",
